{"authored" [{"question" "q-125460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ Interpret circulation as the sum of the four convergent improper line integrals over the open quadrant arcs, taking independent one-sided limits at $(0,\\pm1)$ and $(\\pm1,0)$. Equivalently, integrate the continuous extension of the scalar pullback $F(r(t))\\cdot r\\prime(t)$. The field itself remains undefined at the four axis intersections, so the original ordinary circulation is undefined." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125460/review.json" "file_sha256" "b9d17dc8fd973ab8ff9b99e1fd5717e6e73ebdb0705475fccd90c91bf9decf82" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125460/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "1880f6dff0ff022eabf8dcc69fb63b630f2e9d1e613456375eb9cbb0f43a14c4" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125460/verification.json" "basis" 2155 "rationale" "Separately reviewed explicit improper-integral correction. Authentic same-topic singular-field grades support the expected source key only; their unqualified ordinary prompts remain mathematically invalid. This correction independently makes the request well-posed."} {"question" "q-125460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The field is undefined where $x=0$ or $y=0$, and the unit circle passes through four such points. Thus the original ordinary circulation is undefined. Under the stated improper-integral convention, the given parameterization is clockwise and\n\n$$r(t)=(\\sin t,\\cos t),\\qquad r\\prime(t)=(\\cos t,-\\sin t).$$\n\nOn each open quadrant arc, both coordinates are nonzero, so\n\n$$F(r(t))\\cdot r\\prime(t)=\\frac{5}{\\cos t}\\cos t+\\left(-\\frac{5}{\\sin t}\\right)(-\\sin t)=10.$$\n\nEvery one-sided endpoint limit of this scalar pullback is $10$. Each arc integral converges absolutely, independently of the other arcs. With $a_k=k\\pi/2$,\n\n$$\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{imp}}=\\sum_{k=0}^{3}\\lim_{\\epsilon_k\\downarrow0,\\,\\delta_k\\downarrow0}\\int_{a_k+\\epsilon_k}^{a_{k+1}-\\delta_k}10\\,dt=4(5\\pi)=20\\pi.$$\n\nThis also equals the integral of the scalar pullback extended continuously by $10$ at its missing points. Only the scalar pullback is extended; the vector field is not assigned finite limits there. No principal-value cancellation or application of Green's theorem is needed." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125460/review.json" "file_sha256" "b9d17dc8fd973ab8ff9b99e1fd5717e6e73ebdb0705475fccd90c91bf9decf82" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125460/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "1880f6dff0ff022eabf8dcc69fb63b630f2e9d1e613456375eb9cbb0f43a14c4" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125460/verification.json" "basis" 2155 "rationale" "Separately reviewed explicit improper-integral correction. Authentic same-topic singular-field grades support the expected source key only; their unqualified ordinary prompts remain mathematically invalid. This correction independently makes the request well-posed."} {"question" "q-125460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20\\pi "] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125460/review.json" "file_sha256" "b9d17dc8fd973ab8ff9b99e1fd5717e6e73ebdb0705475fccd90c91bf9decf82" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125460/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "1880f6dff0ff022eabf8dcc69fb63b630f2e9d1e613456375eb9cbb0f43a14c4" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125460/verification.json" "basis" 2155 "rationale" "Separately reviewed explicit improper-integral correction. Authentic same-topic singular-field grades support the expected source key only; their unqualified ordinary prompts remain mathematically invalid. This correction independently makes the request well-posed."} {"question" "q-125460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "e447b779127c795b61ced2b08593b8b69fe8aa6861da93939080762eb3aba40a" "basis" 2154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =5+5 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }10\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =10t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =10(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =20\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "e447b779127c795b61ced2b08593b8b69fe8aa6861da93939080762eb3aba40a" "basis" 2154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "db28b0a7b5c742355e8580b2967546f571e77d3e2c41d730513aea8b33728364" "basis" 2154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "e447b779127c795b61ced2